course: dictionary
lesson: 15284
title: Sincerity: meaning what you say
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sincerity means being honest and meaning what you say or feel. A sincere person is not pretending. «Mia said sorry and looked her brother in the eye.» Her face and her words match, so her apology shows sincerity.
explain: Sincerity can be seen in actions as well as words. «Sam's thank-you card had drawings he made just for Grandma.» All that effort shows his thanks is real, not just polite words.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it in: «Mia's apology was honest and real.» If that still fits the sentence, you have the right meaning. Phrases such as «in all sincerity» tell you the speaker is being completely honest.
fact: Sincerity is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say «sincerity», not «sincerities».
fact: «Sincerity» means being honest and meaning what you say or feel.
fact: «Sincere» is the adjective: a sincere apology is one that is honest and real.
fact: In the UK, letters often end «Yours sincerely»; in the USA, people often write «Sincerely».
fact: Useful phrases: «in all sincerity», «with sincerity», and «doubt someone's sincerity», which means to think someone may not be honest.
exercise: «Mia said sorry and looked her brother in the eye, and she really meant it.» What does this show about Mia? | She is very loud and cheerful | She is pretending to feel sorry | *Her apology is honest and sincere | She has forgotten what she did
exercise: «Dad doubted the sincerity of the boy's promise, because he had broken three before.» What does doubted the sincerity mean? | Dad had forgotten the promise | Dad wanted a bigger promise | *Dad did not think the promise was really honest | Dad was sure the boy was telling the truth
exercise: In the UK, a formal letter often ends with which words? | Your best friend forever | *Yours sincerely | Pardon me | Bye bye for now
test: Which sentence shows sincerity best? | «Sorry, whatever.» | *«I am sorry I was unkind, and I mean it.» | «I said sorry, but I was laughing.»
test: «Sara's compliment was not sincere; she was only being polite.» What does this tell you? | Sara was angry with her friend | Sara meant every word she said | *Sara did not really mean it; she was just being polite | Sara felt very sad that day
exam: What does sincerity mean? | Being quick at running races | Being famous and well known | Being very tired after a long day | *Being honest and meaning what you say or feel
